{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/156965-literary-characters-as-d-d-character-classes","id":156965,"title":"Literary characters as D&D Character Classes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-02T15:57:36-07:00","id":156965,"title":"Literary characters as D&D Character Classes?","content":"Stupid question, but this occurred to me earlier: If you were to build a classic Adventuring Party in the D&amp;D style, *out of Pulp Characters*, who would best fit what roles?<br /> <br /> Some are easy:<br /> <br /> Conan would be the Fighter. Elric would be the Wizard. But who would you choose for the Thief and Cleric? Bard or Paladin?<br /> <br /> I was thinking of mainly pulp characters, but if you want to widen the possibilities to more recent literature, other genres, or even ancient mythology/legends, then go nuts!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T18:58:25-07:00","id":157242,"title":"","content":"Um..I thought Elric was a wizard/fighter (in the old D&amp;D book). Solomon Kane could be a paladin maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-sha